\title{LeeDiD: Bounds on Intensive Margin Treatment Effects in Panel Data}
\description{
Implements the identification and estimation strategy of Viviens (2026) for the intensive margin treatment effect in panel data settings. Adapts the Horowitz-Manski-Lee bounds to the Changes-in-Changes framework to partially identify the average and quantile treatment effect on the treated among 'Always Observed' units, leveraging multiple sources of sample selection jointly to relax the monotonicity assumption behind the original bounds. Provides point estimates, bootstrap standard errors, and Imbens-Manski confidence intervals for the resulting identified sets.
